<title>USA: Electricidade de Portugal's stock soars on first day of trading.</title>
<headline>Electricidade de Portugal's stock soars on first day of trading.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The stock of Portugal's national electric company, Electricidade de Portugal, shot up more than 33 percent in its first day of U.S. trading Tuesday.</p>
<p>EDP's stock was up $8.53125 at $34.375 on heavy volume of nearly 3 million shares on the New York Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>The Portuguese government sold a 30 percent stake in a first-stage privatisation of EDP-Electricidade.</p>
<p>The global offering of 150 million shares was priced at $25.84 per share.</p>
